    "title": "Visit This Outdoor Museum In Indiana Where The 1800s Come Alive - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Madison White ,\n1 days ago The smell of wood smoke hits you first, followed by the sound of a hammer striking an anvil somewhere in the distance. Welcome to Conner Prairie in Fishers, Indiana, where the 19th century isn’t just preserved; it’s actively happening all around you. This isn’t one of those museums... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
